# The test-kernel option ledger.  A kernel built with any option listed here
# is a test kernel: it is never packaged, published or placed on release
# media.  This file is the one list of those options.  Its readers:
#
#   release/scripts/check-test-kernel.sh   refuses kernels and modules that
#                                          carry a row's marker or symbol
#                                          prefix (the check that decides);
#   usr.sbin/bsd-build (build-bsd)         reads it from the source tree at
#                                          run time and refuses a package or
#                                          media plan whose configuration
#                                          names a row's option;
#   usr.sbin/bsd-build/tests               test_options_test checks that the
#                                          tree agrees with it (config(8)
#                                          sweep, options, markers);
#   tools/build/fuchsia/vm-provider.sh     reports a guest's test knobs.
#
# One row per option, six fields separated by "|", no spaces around them:
#
#   option     the config(8) option name ([A-Z0-9_]);
#   status     "live": the option exists in sys/conf/options and its code
#              carries the marker; "reserved": the name and marker are
#              fixed here for a design that has not landed, and no code
#              or configuration may use them yet;
#   config     the one configuration in the tree allowed to name the
#              option (a file name under sys/<arch>/conf), or "-" for none;
#   prefix     a symbol prefix that only the option's code uses, or "-";
#   marker     the "@(#)5BSD ..." string the option's code carries;
#   knobs      the sysctl names the option adds, comma-separated, or "-".
#
# Adding a row is enough for build-bsd, the check script and the runner.  A
# live row's marker and prefix must never occur in a kernel built without
# the option: the check reads kernels as bytes, including CTF and sysctl
# descriptions.
#
